{
  "esm": "1.2.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "rates-retrofit-base-runspec",
    "description": "PLAN.md §7.3.80: `rates-retrofit-base`, the un-retrofitted twin of `rates-retrofit` -- the same RunSpec without its user input database: THC, CO, NMHC and the PM2.5 total with EC, NonECPM, sulfate and aerosol water at running and start exhaust, for the single-unit short-haul truck (52) and the combination long-haul truck (62), every fuel MOVES adds, in Washtenaw County, DEFAULT domain, August 2020, weekday, hour 7, at `<modelscale value=\"Rates\"/>`, from the default database alone.\n\nWHAT IT DISCRIMINATES. RatePerDistance for cohorts of SEVERAL regulatory classes on the per-speed-bin path (finding F91): 52 gasoline (classes 41, 42, 46, 47), 52 diesel (41, 42, 46, 47) and 62 diesel (46, 47, 49), beside single-class CNG. BaseRateCalculator weights each class's per-bin emissionRate by its share of the cohort's source-bin activity (`smfrRatesFraction`, `rt_regClassRateShare`) before BaseRateOutput sums the classes; without it RatePerDistance was 1.9x to 112x high at the multi-class model years. With no retrofit row `rt_retrofitFactor` is exactly 1, so this run checks the class weighting with the retrofit factor out of the product; beside `rates-retrofit` it is also the twin the retrofit port's factors were measured against (PLAN.md §7.3.79).\n\nTHE BINDINGS. `n_ratesScale` = 1 and `n_outputRate`, the (pollutant-process, road type, cohort) pairs across five road types, checked by `rateSurvivorCount`; `n_sourceBin` 8 and `n_physicsRow` 41, as in `rates-retrofit`.",
    "authors": [
      "EarthSciML Authors and Contributors"
    ],
    "tags": [
      "runspec",
      "onroad",
      "default-database",
      "rates",
      "multi-bin"
    ]
  },
